      "message": "[From Jetski review] Nit: A non-default GN toolchain named `toolchain(\"action\")` emits `rule action_cc`, `rule action_cxx`, `rule action_link`, etc. in its `toolchain.ninja` (`GetNinjaRulePrefixForToolchain` + lowercase tool name), which would shadow `rule action_cc` in that subninja scope if a Starlark action uses `mnemonic \u003d \"CC\"`. Keeping `mnemonic` uppercase here (e.g. `rule action_TOOL` / `rule action_CC`, since built-in GN tool names are always lowercase) or using a distinct prefix like `starlark_action_` (or `__starlark_action_`) would avoid any collision and also avoid the `to_lowercase()` `String` allocation.",
